# Dynamic Move Time for AI/Impossible Mode

## Background

Currently, the Stockfish engine uses **fixed timeout budgets** per difficulty level:
- Advanced: 5000ms
- Impossible: 5000ms  
- AI Mode: 7000ms

These fixed values mean the AI takes the same amount of time whether it's a simple forced recapture or a deep middlegame calculation — leading to unnecessary wait times on "obvious" positions.

The user wants the AI to **move fast when the position is simple and take more time only when needed**, while keeping Beginner/Intermediate modes untouched (they already use Sunfish with fixed settings).

## Proposed Changes

### Design: Leela-Inspired Dynamic Move Time

After the player makes a move, the system already performs a **background analysis** of the player's move (lines 1410-1437 in game_bloc.dart). This analysis updates the AI personality. We'll extend this to also **compute a position complexity score** that directly feeds into the Stockfish movetime, creating a dynamic, personality-aware time budget.

**Key Principle**: If Stockfish returns a valid move quickly (depth reached, forced line), it should emit it immediately without wasting the full budget. The `movetime` UCI parameter already does this — Stockfish will stop early if it's confident. We just need to set smarter initial budgets.

### Complexity Scoring Formula

```
Complexity Score = weighted sum of:
  - Legal moves count (more options = more complex)
  - Pieces on board (more pieces = more complex middlegame)
  - Personality urgency (aggressive personality wants to move faster)  
  - Whether position is a forced line (check/single legal move → instant)
```

**Move Time Mapping** (Advanced/Impossible/AI Mode):
| Complexity | Move Time | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Forced (1 legal move / recapture) | 300-500ms | Only one legal move, just play it |
| Simple (< 15 legal moves, few pieces) | 800-1500ms | Endgame, clear plan |
| Medium (15-30 legal moves) | 1500-3000ms | Typical middlegame |
| Complex (30+ legal moves, all pieces) | 3000-5000ms (adv/imp) / 3000-7000ms (ai) | Complex middlegame |

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Beginner and Intermediate modes are completely unchanged** — they continue using Sunfish with their existing fixed settings.

### Personality-Driven Time Modifier

The personality engine already switches between aggressive/defensive/tricky after each move analysis. We'll apply a time multiplier:

- **Aggressive** → 0.7x (moves faster, more impulsive)
- **Defensive** → 1.0x (takes full time to be careful)
- **Tricky** → 0.85x (medium speed, setting traps)

