## How It Works End-to-End

```
Player makes move
  → Background analysis runs (existing) → personality adapts
  → GameAIRequestEvent fires
  → engine_controller.getBestMove() called
  → _getSmartMove() computes complexity:
      - Count legal moves from engine
      - Count pieces on board  
      - Get personality time multiplier
      - Compute: baseTime = f(complexity)
      - Apply: moveTime = baseTime * personalityMultiplier
      - Clamp to [300ms, maxCap]
  → Passes moveTime to JS bridge
  → engine_service.js uses moveTime as budget (capped by safety max)
  → Stockfish worker gets `go depth X movetime Y`
  → Stockfish returns bestmove (often before budget expires)
  → Move played immediately
```

> [!NOTE]  
> Stockfish's `movetime` parameter already means "take *up to* this long". If it finds a clear best move at depth 8, it won't wait until the full movetime expires. So setting a smart initial budget is mostly about avoiding unnecessarily long *worst case* waits.

